---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Work & Projects — Joey Hershkop" 
  description="Selected software engineering projects, production systems, and case studies by Joey Hershkop."
>
  <h2>Selected Work &amp; Case Studies</h2>
  <p class="lead-text">
    A selection of production systems, open-source data pipelines, and full-stack software architecture.
  </p>

  <div class="work-list">
    <article class="work-item">
      <h3><a href="/work/parkking/" class="text-link">Parkking — Toronto Street Parking Intelligence Platform</a></h3>
      <p>
        An end-to-end geospatial system turning 76,849 rows of unstructured Toronto parking bylaws into 21,433 geocoded curb segments with instant offline verdicts across mobile and web:
      </p>
      <ul class="work-subcomponents">
        <li><strong>Spatial ETL &amp; NLP Pipeline (Python):</strong> Parses freeform legal text for temporal rules and geographic spans, resolves street intersections via Toronto Centreline graph search, and projects spans onto physical road edges using Shapely.</li>
        <li><strong>Native iOS Client (SwiftUI &amp; MapKit):</strong> Zero-dependency, offline-first mobile app featuring an instant curb bylaw evaluation engine and 60/120 fps viewport polyline batching.</li>
        <li><strong>Interactive Web App (TypeScript &amp; MapLibre):</strong> Mobile-first browser map for instant parking inspection, time scrubbing, and address lookup.</li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="work-tags" aria-label="Technologies used">
        <li>Python</li>
        <li>GeoPandas &amp; Shapely</li>
        <li>SwiftUI</li>
        <li>MapKit</li>
        <li>TypeScript</li>
        <li>React &amp; MapLibre</li>
        <li>Spatial ETL</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="work-links">
        <a href="/work/parkking/">Read Case Study &rarr;</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/JoeHershkie/parkking-pipeline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pipeline Repo &rarr;</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/JoeHershkie/parkking-ios" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">iOS Repo &rarr;</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/JoeHershkie/parkking-web" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Web Repo &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="work-item">
      <h3><a href="/work/stripe-billing/" class="text-link">B2B SaaS Stripe Billing &amp; Ingestion Engine</a></h3>
      <p>
        Owned end-to-end subscription billing for a live B2B SaaS platform: raw HTTP body preservation middleware for HMAC signature verification, idempotent webhook processing to prevent replay attacks, and PostgreSQL state mirroring.
      </p>
      <ul class="work-tags" aria-label="Technologies used">
        <li>PHP</li>
        <li>PostgreSQL</li>
        <li>Stripe API</li>
        <li>Webhooks</li>
        <li>Security</li>
        <li>React</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="work-links">
        <a href="/work/stripe-billing/">Read Case Study &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="work-item">
      <h3><a href="/work/reggeee/" class="text-link">Reggeee — Greenfield Family Activity Marketplace</a></h3>
      <p>
        Architected a two-sided marketplace from scratch: designed the PostgreSQL schema modeling non-traditional multi-adult families (divorced co-parents, guardians), built Argon2id auth with anti-enumeration protection, Redis session state, and a typed React 19 frontend.
      </p>
      <ul class="work-tags" aria-label="Technologies used">
        <li>React 19</li>
        <li>TypeScript</li>
        <li>Slim 4</li>
        <li>PostgreSQL</li>
        <li>Redis</li>
        <li>Argon2id</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="work-links">
        <a href="/work/reggeee/">Read Case Study &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="work-item">
      <h3><a href="/work/realtime-pipeline/" class="text-link">Event-Driven Realtime Pipeline</a></h3>
      <p>
        Engineered an event-driven pub/sub synchronization bridge using Ably that connects backend webhook mutations to frontend React Query state within milliseconds via automated query invalidation.
      </p>
      <ul class="work-tags" aria-label="Technologies used">
        <li>Ably</li>
        <li>Pub/Sub</li>
        <li>TanStack Query</li>
        <li>TypeScript</li>
        <li>PHP</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="work-links">
        <a href="/work/realtime-pipeline/">Read Case Study &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="work-item">
      <h3>Auditable Documents Platform &amp; In-Browser Viewer</h3>
      <p>
        Built an end-to-end document sharing and review platform for collaborative B2B organization views. Implemented in-browser previews across PDF, image, and DOCX formats, append-only sharing audit ledgers, file conflict resolution flows, and Playwright e2e suites.
      </p>
      <ul class="work-tags" aria-label="Technologies used">
        <li>React</li>
        <li>TypeScript</li>
        <li>PostgreSQL</li>
        <li>DOCX / PDF Preview</li>
        <li>Playwright</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="work-links">
        <a href="/resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View in Resume &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="work-item">
      <h3>HoverBot — Vision-Based Navigation System</h3>
      <p>
        Authored a multithreaded computer-vision navigation pipeline in Python using OpenCV and NumPy, sustaining 30 fps with &le; 100 ms image-to-actuation latency and &plusmn; 3 cm mean arrival error across 30 physical waypoints.
      </p>
      <ul class="work-tags" aria-label="Technologies used">
        <li>Python</li>
        <li>OpenCV</li>
        <li>NumPy</li>
        <li>Threading</li>
        <li>Robotics</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="work-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/JoeHershkie" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Profile &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
